FINAL ANSWER:
Troy Goode is the single contributor behind `lib/` and `test/`. No one person holds more than half of the whole repository.

These numbers count surviving lines, from `git blame -w -M -C -C`, on `HEAD`. They cover 18 files and 1,985 of 1,995 lines. The unit is lines, not commits or knowledge.

**Whole repository**
- Bus factor is 2. Troy Goode and Douglas Christopher Wilson together hold 72.5% of the lines. Reaching 80% takes 4 authors.
- Troy Goode: 810 lines (40.8%) and 95 commits (30.2%).
- Douglas Christopher Wilson: 629 lines (31.7%) and 143 commits (45.4%).
- Next are Íñigo Marquínez Prado with 95 lines (4.8%) and Jon Church with 72 (3.6%). 52 more authors hold the rest.

**By directory, where one person holds more than half**

| Directory | Bus factor | Who | Share |
|---|---|---|---|
| `lib/` (1 file, 238 lines) | 1 | Troy Goode: 159 lines | 66.8% |
| `test/` (7 files, 966 lines) | 1 | Troy Goode: 517 lines | 53.5% |

Douglas Christopher Wilson holds only 9.2% of `lib/` (22 lines), so he is not a backup there. In `test/` he holds 38.7% (374 lines).

**Directories that are not single-person**
- The root files (6 files, 415 lines) have a bus factor of 2. Troy Goode holds 32.3%, Douglas Christopher Wilson 27.7% and Jon Church 17.3%.
- `.github/` (4 files, 366 lines) has a bus factor of 2. Douglas Christopher Wilson holds 32.2% and Íñigo Marquínez Prado 26.0%.

**Caveats**
- **Identity merge (a guess):** I counted `<email redacted>` (762 lines, 93 commits) and `troy@laptop.example` (48 lines, 2 commits) as one person. The evidence is the same name only. Unmerged, the gmail address alone has 762 lines (38.4%), so the conclusion holds either way. I wrote nothing to `.mailmap`.
- **Reformat commit left out:** `62628c0` ("style: reformat js with 4-space indent and double quotes", Fiona Formatter, 2026-04-12) only changed whitespace and quotes. The tool left it out of the numbers above. With it counted, Fiona Formatter would hold 291 lines (14.7%), Troy Goode 715 (36.0%) and Douglas Christopher Wilson 454 (22.9%). The bus factor stays 2.
- **Bots left out:** 1 bot identity (10 lines, 11 commits) is excluded.
- **Limits of the method:** These figures don't show review work, design discussions or code that was deleted. A high share of lines is not the same as being the only person who understands the code.
- **Suggested action:** Have someone other than Troy Goode review changes to `lib/`, and spread `test/` reviews beyond Troy Goode too.

